    <!-- Dialogs -->
    <string name="dialog_guide_title">ℹ️ Android TV Restricted Settings</string>
    <string name="dialog_guide_msg">On Android TV and Google TV, app settings do not have the 3-dot menu found on phones.

Therefore, TvAfrTools unlocks permissions automatically:

1. Make sure "USB Debugging" is enabled in Developer Options on your TV.
2. Click "⚡ Auto-activate in 1 click".
3. If a confirmation dialog appears on your TV, check "Always allow" and press OK with your remote.</string>
    <string name="dialog_auto_setup_title">⚡ Activating permissions on your TV</string>
    <string name="dialog_auto_setup_msg">Connecting to internal ADB system...

👉 IMPORTANT: If a prompt appears on your TV asking to allow USB debugging, check Always allow and press OK with your remote.</string>
    <string name="dialog_ready_title">✓ All set!</string>
    <string name="dialog_ready_msg">Remote permissions and the display refresh rate engine are now active. You can start using your configured buttons.</string>
    <string name="dialog_auth_popup_title">Accept the prompt on your TV</string>
    <string name="dialog_failed_title">Could not activate automatically</string>
    <string name="dialog_auth_popup_msg">A confirmation window has appeared on your TV.

1. Check Always allow from this computer
2. Press OK with your remote

Once accepted, click Retry.</string>
